Stellar catalogue (ephemeris/sefstars.txt.xz)
------------------------------------------
Compiled by Fabio Silva from the SIMBAD database, operated at CDS,
Strasbourg, France, and supplemented with SIMBAD records and Johnson V
magnitudes from the Hipparcos catalogue through CDS/VizieR.

This catalogue contains SIMBAD-derived information and is distributed under
the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0. This notice applies to the combined
catalogue, including the original compilation and subsequent additions.
https://simbad.cds.unistra.fr/simbad/
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
Reference: Wenger et al. (2000), The SIMBAD astronomical database,
A&AS 143, 9. https://doi.org/10.1051/aas:2000332

Additional Johnson V magnitudes: ESA (1997), The Hipparcos and Tycho
Catalogues, ESA SP-1200; CDS/VizieR I/239/hip_main (Vmag).
https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/cat/I/239
This work uses the VizieR catalogue access tool, CDS, Strasbourg, France
(DOI: 10.26093/cds/vizier).

The catalogue is formatted for Swiss Ephemeris and stored with lossless xz
compression. It is expanded into session-temporary storage without changing
its values. It is not a copy of the standard Swiss Ephemeris catalogue.

For the additions retrieved on 4 November 2026, the machine-readable
supplement, source queries and conversion script are supplied in the source
repository (data-raw/simbad-2026-11-04). The field-reference table is also
installed in ephemeris/. These materials retain ODbL 1.0.
The supplement adds 59 stellar records and identifies existing 39 Com A as
HIP 63948 without changing that record's numeric values. Other original
catalogue records are unchanged. SIMBAD ICRS coordinates are at epoch J2000;
proper motion in RA includes cos(dec), in mas/year; declination motion is in
mas/year, parallax in mas, radial velocity in km/s. Angles are converted to
sexagesimal only. Hipparcos Vmag is used where SIMBAD has no V magnitude;
Hipparcos J1991.25 positions are NOT copied as J2000 coordinates.
HIP 108797 uses SIMBAD's Hipparcos-2007 measurement-table PM/parallax values
(2007A&A...474..653V), matching the coordinate reference. Five unavailable
radial velocities use explicitly documented zero placeholders, not measured
values: HIP 4714, 51734, 72181, 79634 and 114164. Per-record references,
retrieval date and assumptions are in star-supplement-2026-11-04.csv.
No star position or magnitude was guessed. Missing spectral types remain ~.

