Malta data
----------
Fabio Silva and Tore Lomsdalen (2025). 'No easy way from the earth to the
stars': a new statistical approach to the orientation of the Maltese temples.
Archaeological and Anthropological Sciences 17, 96.
https://doi.org/10.1007/s12520-025-02208-4
The publication is CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
It reports that all study datasets are available as supplementary information.
The entrance measurements have been reformatted for R. The bundled horizon
profiles are derived research data, not a redistribution of the underlying
raw elevation raster. The maintainer confirmed permission for the bundled
Malta datasets on 4 November 2026. That confirmation is recorded separately
from the paper's licence, which does not automatically license third-party
material excluded by a credit line. Existing dataset documentation retains
survey and horizon-generation provenance. Lossless compression does not
change the values or precision of these datasets.

Chinese constellation figures (chinese and chinese_mansions sets)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Source: Stellarium 0.22.2, skycultures/chinese.
https://github.com/Stellarium/stellarium/tree/v0.22.2/skycultures/chinese
Licence declaration: info.ini, CC BY-SA 4.0 International Public License.
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Credit: Karrie Berglund (Digitalis Education Solutions, Inc.), Sun Shuwei,
and Stellarium contributors. Upstream also acknowledges Liu Chunbin's
catalogue collation and Hong Kong Space Museum's English-Chinese glossary.
Historical sources include Yi Shitong (1981), Chinese and Western Contrast
Star Chart and Catalogue 1950.0; imperial Yixiang kaocheng catalogues;
and Pan Nai, The History of Stellar Observation in China.
Adaptation: all 318 line-file records and their English/pinyin labels are
repackaged as an R data frame, identifiers prefixed CHN. The 28 lunar-mansion
asterisms are also extracted and ordered Horn to Chariot as a separate set.
Endpoints are unchanged, including six empty records and single-star figures.
No artwork, sector boundaries, or upstream stellar position catalogue is included.
These adapted data retain CC BY-SA 4.0, separately from the package GPL code.

Star-name lookup (star.names)
-----------------------------
Stellar proper names: International Astronomical Union Working Group on Star
Names, IAU Catalog of Star Names.
https://exopla.net/star-names/modern-iau-star-names/
The 304-entry lookup also contains non-stellar object names. It is distinct
from the astrometric catalogue. Fabio Silva manually transcribed the stellar
names from an IAU table. The exact table version, extraction date and a separate
licence declaration for that compilation are not recorded locally.

Milky Way tracing (extdata/milky-way-layers.rds; earlier outline: milky-way.csv)
---------------------------------------------------
Adapted from diffuse stellar light in Deep Star Maps 2020.
https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4851/
Credit: NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center Scientific Visualization Studio;
ESA/Gaia/DPAC. This is an illustrative outline, not the source image or a
prediction of visibility. It does not reconstruct the Galaxy's evolution.

